{
  "abstract": "Eliminating the global reverse-depth sweep of backpropagation is a central goal in neuromorphic computing, but conventional forward perturbation rules incur estimator variance scaling with parameter count $\\mathcal{O}(|\\Theta|/K)$ or hidden width $\\mathcal{O}(M/K)$. Adapting Stephen Chung's Weight Maximization and Sylvester-Hadamard exploration, we study parameter-space column contraction over an $S$-token micro-horizon (`WM-S` and `Co-WM-S`). Under fixed downstream targets, column isolation replaces sibling-neuron cross-talk with $S$-token cross-talk, and sampling $K$ distinct Hadamard columns reduces conditional variance by $\\frac{S-K}{K(S-1)}$, vanishing at $K=S$. We separate strict no-backward methods (`local_reverse_derivative_calls=0`, `hub_mode=\"dust_hub\"`) from hybrid local-hub-pullback controls (`local_reverse_derivative_calls=L=6`, `hub_mode=\"co_wm_s\"`, reconstructing $\\widehat{E}_g = U_g W_O$ across $W_O$) and block-local reverse-credit controls. First, we establish a two-stage faithful baseline of published DUST (Stage 1: `max_grad_diff=0.0` suffix-cache equivalence, $1.75\\times$ speedup; Stage 2: $2.37697\\pm 0.06975$ holdout BPB under SGD $P=64$, $2.24921\\pm 0.00044$ under Muon $P=64$, and $2.10883\\pm 0.00138$ at $P=256$ on ClimbMix `d6`) alongside Fairly Optimized DUST (`sc+sh`, $2.04590\\pm 0.00012$ at $P=64$). Second, we introduce Strict No-Backward `Delayed-Trace-Co-WM-S` (`delayed_trace_cowm_*`, `rev=0`), combining SRAM-fused outgoing-column contractions (`_outgoing_col_dot_all8_kernel`, $18.7\\text{ ms}$ across 6 layers at $M=4096$) on `mlp.c_proj` $\\to$ `mlp.c_fc` with full-hub covariance centering (`hub2`, `hubs=[2,2,2,2,2,2]`) and intra-block branch decoupling (`bd025`), using $0$ `hidden` suffix forwards and $0$ reverse/pullback matmuls. Across Regime I fixed-$D=256$ MLP-width scaling ($2$ seeds, $M \\in \\{256, 1024, 4096\\}$) and Regime II full-model width scaling ($D \\in \\{128, 256, 384, 512\\}, M=4D$), Strict No-Backward `Delayed-Trace-Co-WM-S` (`rev=0`) achieves descriptive gains over unmodified and Fairly Optimized DUST at all widths while running faster ($-0.01107\\text{ BPB}$ and $92.7\\text{ ms/step}$ faster at $M=4096$), and on 2-seed `d6` reaches $2.04412\\pm 0.00014\\text{ BPB}$ in $633.6\\text{s}/635.2\\text{s}$ (vs $2.04590\\pm 0.00012$ at $648.0\\text{s}/649.3\\text{s}$ at $P=64$) and $2.08637\\pm 0.01282\\text{ BPB}$ in $294.9\\text{s}/297.9\\text{s}$ at $P=256$ (vs $2.11372\\pm 0.00121$ at $302.0\\text{s}/306.2\\text{s}$). Checkpointed backpropagation retains superior efficiency ($1.45179\\text{ BPB}$, $33.3\\text{ ms}$).",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Revision for version 6 resolving all three qualifications from the accepted v5 review (LxzR7ggbNnIJU-eR): (1) Separated the value-pooling estimator effect from the local (q,k) allocation change in Table 10 (`test_recency_vtrace_and_subspace_writers.py` and `recency_vtrace_and_subspace_diagnostic.json`): holding `(q, k) = (1, 4)` matched to `delayed_trace_cowm_P64_hub2_bd025_sc_sh_d1` (`2.12965` BPB), 200-step ClimbMix `d6` holdout BPB improves from `2.16374` (`(q, k) = (4, 7)`) to `2.14681` (`610.6 ms`) at gamma=1.00 and `2.14782` (`607.7 ms`) at gamma=0.98 (via exact 1-pass FlashAttention rescaling `w_t^{-1} w_tau = gamma^{t-tau}`), demonstrating that `+0.01693 BPB` (49.7%) of the `+0.03409 BPB` gap came from changing `(q, k)` to `(4, 7)`. Direct R=16 Monte Carlo variance/cosine/effective-rank measurements on a 50-step ClimbMix `d6` state further show that under 2-draw forward hub targets (`hubs=[2,2,2,2,2,2]`), gamma=1.00 value pooling achieves higher single-trial cosine (`0.0587, 0.0376, 0.0726` at Layers 0, 2, 5) and lower relative variance (`14.39, 14.53, 13.13`) than both gamma=0.98 value pooling (`0.0389, 0.0244, 0.0505`) and DUST's `local_errors('v')` (`0.0068, 0.0003, 0.0095`, `rel_var=14.96-15.02`), and that the remaining `+0.01716 BPB` gap stems from spectral rank compression of the attention-smoothed outer product (`single_trial_erank = 88.3-127.3` vs `191.1-218.4` for `local_errors('v')`) prior to Muon's Newton-Schulz (`NS5`) update; (2) Restored `run_neuronal_scaling_pretrain.py` (imported by `run_pure_forward_only_suite.py`) into `supplement.zip`, added `test_recency_vtrace_and_subspace_writers.py`, and added the CLI mode aliases `regime1_mlp_scaling` and `innovation_screen` directly to `argparse` `choices` in `run_dust_and_delayed_trace_suite.py`; and (3) Explicitly stated in Table 9 and Section 4.1 that the matched-wall-clock winners are combined package comparisons and that `Complete s` (`total_cum_train_s`) sums all training steps 0..N-1 excluding validation-evaluation and checkpoint-writing overhead.",
